reviewers.overall_notes:
I reviewed batch_07: 20 cards, all three views each, every line read. Card ranks run 7 to 254. The batch has 4 no-leak cards, 1 contact card with no leaks (Norby), 1 video-only plan (Gilbert), 1 switch hitter who was also traded (Bailey), 1 noted hitter (Clement) and 4 execution-led cards. The roster rows match their cards on Top leak, Leak runs, Beat and Start with for every hitter.

Main problems, worst first:

(1) The hand tabs are put together from mixed sources:
- markers stay on the all-pitchers leaks while the list and the 'leak N' tags are renumbered;
- the coach's note says 'the plan's first line' on tabs with a different first line;
- the contact and good-chooser lines quote card-level numbers, and spread lines quote the hand's share as 'a season';
- a 'mostly vs RHP' leak can vanish from the vs RHP tab (Crow-Armstrong's 4.6-run top leak, Díaz's only plan line);
- Jung's vs RHP tab both prescribes takes and says there are none.

(2) The order rule (pre-two-strike takes first) often makes a 12-24 pitch leak the first line, drops a leak 2-3x bigger, and leaves the table's costliest count with no line. The framing line does not catch this because coverage is measured against the net choices loss (Griffin's ahead-in-count −4.0, Contreras's first pitch −2.2 and 0-1/1-1 −2.0). House's vs RHP spread line names three costly counts and calls a two-strike pitch the biggest piece of them.

(3) Numbers that disagree in print:
- 62% in the plan vs 63% in the list, from Python and JS rounding 0.5 differently (21 leak rates page-wide; plan_checks misses it);
- the picture hover's bold gap is not the difference of the two rates shown under it, and the 3D view prints a different 'you';
- target points are 4-14 below what the leak rows add up to, and for Torkelson the sign flips ('1 points below').

(4) Markers sit on blue or gray spots, because the pictures blend pitch types and the leaks do not.

One false lead: the dossier shows some leak numbers as '3' rather than '(3)'. That comes from format_dossiers.py's regex skipping names that start with a digit ('0-1 or 1-1'); the page itself is fine. I did not have phone or dark-mode renders for this batch, so layout findings are limited to text.

issues.method:
I ran skeptic_boilerplate/measure.py over all 261 players in dump_2026.json (plan_items, plan_items_by_hand, leaks, tables) and over the aside text of all three views. It measures:
- the caption under "None worth";
- plans whose tagged leak numbers skip a bigger leak;
- words per pitch line and per plan, and which clauses each line carries;
- count-phrase repeats, exact and mixed;
- the "When you're ahead," opener vs the "in the count" opener, on cards and in the roster's Start with column;
- region and pitch words in the plan vs the leak's region and pitch group;
- fallback lines vs the count table.

check_reported.py tested each reported card against its own finding's pattern. I re-took two screenshots with shot.mjs (Ward and Cronenworth at 1440 px). I also read the template's aside() function, plan_items, strength_clause, contact_clause, fallback_line, GROUP_WORDS_SHORT and the word tables in step 17, the print-card leak header, and the plus-count check in plan_checks.py.
